WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:04.760
Okay, friends.

00:04.760 --> 00:09.760
So now what we're gonna do, I'm going to show you a quick guide about the GitHub copilot in the Visual

00:09.760 --> 00:10.520
Studio Code.

00:10.520 --> 00:15.840
Once you create a profile and connect it to your Visual Studio, you will get a new icon for the copilot.

00:15.840 --> 00:19.120
So once you go there, you can see quickly the status.

00:19.160 --> 00:21.880
And as well you can go and disable the copilot.

00:21.880 --> 00:25.520
So if you have it like this, that means your copilot is active.

00:25.520 --> 00:29.160
So now once you have everything up and running, what you have to do is very simple.

00:29.320 --> 00:31.720
Just go and start writing your code.

00:31.720 --> 00:34.360
So start typing any select statements.

00:34.360 --> 00:36.760
And now you can see that we have a gray text.

00:36.840 --> 00:39.640
This gray text called the ghost text.

00:39.640 --> 00:42.080
It is an autocompletion from the copilot.

00:42.120 --> 00:45.000
And now it says select star from table.

00:45.040 --> 00:50.520
And now as you can see, as I mouse hover on it, we can see that I can go and switch between different

00:50.520 --> 00:51.440
suggestions.

00:51.440 --> 00:54.040
So here we have like three suggestions 123.

00:54.080 --> 00:56.120
And I'm going to go with the third one.

00:56.120 --> 01:01.480
So now here as it says if you want to accept the suggestion all what you have to do is to press tab.

01:01.520 --> 01:02.720
So let's go and do it.

01:02.720 --> 01:04.760
So you are accepting the whole thing.

01:04.880 --> 01:08.450
But now if you say no what I'm going to accept only part of the code.

01:08.450 --> 01:10.810
So let's go again and write select.

01:10.810 --> 01:12.410
So this time we're going to be selective.

01:12.410 --> 01:16.010
In order to do that hold Ctrl and then with the right arrow.

01:16.250 --> 01:20.450
And with that we are accepting part of the ghost not everything.

01:20.450 --> 01:23.810
But of course if you are accepting the whole thing just go with the tab.

01:23.850 --> 01:27.370
And now there is another way in order to trigger the ghost text.

01:27.490 --> 01:29.610
And that's by defining first a commands.

01:29.610 --> 01:32.690
For example, we want to select the top three customers based on the score.

01:32.730 --> 01:38.650
So now once you start writing the query, the copilot can go and write a query that is relevant for

01:38.650 --> 01:39.450
the comments.

01:39.450 --> 01:44.050
So now as you can see, we are getting top three from customers because we want the top three customers.

01:44.050 --> 01:46.170
And here we have like two suggestions.

01:46.210 --> 01:48.530
Like over here we have the order by or without it.

01:48.530 --> 01:50.610
So I will go with order by and hit tab.

01:50.650 --> 01:54.530
And now here another suggestion which is correct, in order to serve the data from the highest to the

01:54.530 --> 01:55.010
lowest.

01:55.050 --> 01:55.330
All right.

01:55.330 --> 01:56.490
Moving on to the next one.

01:56.490 --> 02:02.250
As we learned in SQL, in order to solve a task, there could be like multiple solutions and multiple

02:02.250 --> 02:05.210
variants of queries that solving the same task.

02:05.210 --> 02:09.370
So let's say that we have this task rank customers based on their total order sales.

02:09.370 --> 02:13.610
So what we can do if we start writing the query we are getting now the ghost text.

02:13.610 --> 02:16.390
But now what we can do, we can go and hit Ctrl enter.

02:16.430 --> 02:18.070
So now what happens on the right side?

02:18.070 --> 02:19.910
You will get different suggestions.

02:19.910 --> 02:23.630
And here we have like nine suggestions on how to solve this task in SQL.

02:23.630 --> 02:27.350
So now what you have to do is to go through all those suggestions and pick one.

02:27.350 --> 02:32.270
For example, I can go with the suggestion number three and say accept suggestion and you will get it

02:32.270 --> 02:33.670
in your code editor.

02:33.670 --> 02:40.230
So this is what we mean with the copilot Autocompletion and integrating the AI directly as you are developing

02:40.230 --> 02:45.390
and writing a code now in the copilot, not only using the ghost text and the Autocompletion, we can

02:45.390 --> 02:48.910
go and interact with the AI using inline chats.

02:48.950 --> 02:50.470
So it's something like ChatGPT.

02:50.590 --> 02:55.230
Now in order to trigger the chat, what you're going to do, you're going to go and hit Ctrl I and then

02:55.230 --> 03:01.110
you're going to get a place in order to ask the copilot any question, like for example, join the query

03:01.150 --> 03:05.270
with the table sales orders.

03:05.630 --> 03:06.910
So let's go and hit it.

03:08.470 --> 03:12.990
And now as you can see, we got a full query where the customers is joined with the orders.

03:12.990 --> 03:15.910
And it is totally correct how the table are joins.

03:15.910 --> 03:22.430
So that means copilot knows already all the tables that I have in the database and as well the columns

03:22.430 --> 03:23.800
and how to join them.

03:23.800 --> 03:24.680
This is amazing.

03:24.680 --> 03:27.160
So if you like it, you go and accept it of course.

03:27.200 --> 03:32.200
And this is way faster than having ChatGPT because in ChatGPT you have to introduce your database,

03:32.200 --> 03:35.720
your columns and stuff before even asking anything.

03:35.920 --> 03:38.840
This is exactly the power of copilot.

03:38.880 --> 03:40.120
Now what else we can do with that?

03:40.120 --> 03:44.120
We can go and highlight part of our code and then start again the charts.

03:44.120 --> 03:50.440
And here we can say replace this column with an aggregation of the sales.

03:51.240 --> 03:52.720
So let's go and hit okay.

03:52.760 --> 03:55.440
Now as you can see it replaced it with an aggregate function.

03:55.440 --> 03:59.280
And one thing that is very important the code is not changed yet.

03:59.280 --> 04:01.960
So it is highlighted and showing you a suggestion.

04:01.960 --> 04:04.160
And now you have to accept it or discard it.

04:04.200 --> 04:06.840
If you discard, nothing can change in your code.

04:06.840 --> 04:10.760
But once you say accept, it's going to go and replace your original code.

04:10.760 --> 04:15.600
So if we go and do that now, your code is replaced with the AI suggestion.

04:15.640 --> 04:20.400
Okay, another thing about the copilot, it's try to fix issues that you have in your code.

04:20.400 --> 04:22.080
So for example we have here an error.

04:22.080 --> 04:27.120
If you go and mouse over it, you can see a menu from the copilot in order to view the error or to fix

04:27.120 --> 04:27.440
it.

04:27.440 --> 04:32.540
And another way to do that, if you right click on it, you go to the copilot and here you can see we

04:32.540 --> 04:34.140
can explain or fix.

04:34.140 --> 04:38.740
So if you go and explain you will get another window where you get an explanation about the issue in

04:38.740 --> 04:39.260
your code.

04:39.260 --> 04:43.140
And once you understand it, you can go and ask the copilot in order to fix it.

04:43.140 --> 04:45.180
So let's go over here and go to fix.

04:46.980 --> 04:49.100
And with that, the copilot did fix the issue.

04:49.140 --> 04:51.940
It was all about the order of the select statements.

04:51.940 --> 04:54.140
So first you have to do the group by then the order by.

04:54.140 --> 04:56.660
So it helps you to find issues and to fix it as well.

04:56.700 --> 05:01.300
And now, as you might already noticed, as we are writing the code and interacting with the Visual

05:01.300 --> 05:07.220
Studio, you will often get a sparkle this little yellow sparkle on the left side, so you will see

05:07.220 --> 05:10.540
this icon each time the copilot thinks it can help.

05:10.540 --> 05:15.380
So if you go and click on it, you will get a menu of different stuff that the copilot can do for you,

05:15.380 --> 05:18.140
like fixing, explaining, modifying, and so on.

05:18.140 --> 05:19.700
Well my friends, that's it.

05:19.700 --> 05:25.020
This is the copilot and it is very simple, but yet very powerful for developers.

05:25.060 --> 05:28.340
And of course, not only for SQL, for anything like for Python and so on.

05:28.380 --> 05:30.140
Everything is integrated in one place.

05:30.140 --> 05:33.220
I don't have to jump to ChatGPT and ask stuff.

05:33.260 --> 05:36.820
It is live and I can do it directly as I'm writing my codes.

05:36.820 --> 05:38.220
So that's all for copilot.
